	)
	(text "Notes: the four channels are identical"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.605 235.204 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(thickness 0.44)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "774f3572-228d-531e-8139-f682deeed38c")
	)
	(text "Channel n: driver U(n+1), fuse Fn, capacitors Cn1-Cn6, fault LED Dn1\n   with Rn1, motor connector J1n.\nMn_IN1..3 are the PWM inputs from the XIAO (page 2).  EN1-3 and nSLEEP\n   are tied high, so each OUT simply follows its IN.\nDRV_EN (XIAO D3, page 2) drives nRESET of all four drivers.  Low = all\n   outputs off; R3 holds it low through boot, reset and flashing.\n   A low pulse also clears a latched fault.\nV3P3 is the chip's own 3.3 V regulator output: Cn6 only.\n   Do NOT join it to the board's +3V3.\nFn (1.1 A hold, 2.2 A trip polyfuse) takes a dead driver off the +12V rail.\nEach channel has its own 100 uF (Cn5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0e20d9a8-b6cc-5f16-9d16-245b2c520aae")
	)
	(text "Cn1 (charge pump, CPL-CPH) must be 50 V rated.  Cn2 is VCP to VM.\nCn3 / Cn4 sit right at the VM pins 4 and 11.\nDn1 lights when the driver reports a fault (nFAULT pulls low).\n   There is no fault line back to the XIAO.\nCOMPP, COMPN, nCOMPO: the comparator is not used and is grounded,\n   as in the TI data sheet.\nEP (pin 29) is the PowerPAD: soldered to the ground pour over vias.\nPWR_FLAG is not a part.  It tells the rule check that a net is\n   powered (a fuse does not count as a source).\nNames on the wires (M1_CPL ...) are the net names used on the PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b0c81dfa-c7c8-5b87-87c7-89bb2e3eb96f")
	)
